  "problem": "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{15}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{3}{10}$ |\n\nLet $Y=-X-6.$ Calculate $P(Y\\le -6).$",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's add a $Y=-X-6$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-2$ | $-4$ | $-6$ | $-8$ | $-10$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{15}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{3}{10}$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, ${f}_{X}(x)={f}_{Y}(y)$ for corresponding values of $X$ and $Y.$ Therefore, the distribution of $Y$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $-2$ | $-4$ | $-6$ | $-8$ | $-10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{1}{15}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{3}{10}$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\le -6) & =\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{1}{10}+\\frac{3}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
